{
  "summary": "Splits the monolithic `CreateNewBlock_validity` miner unit test into four independent `BOOST_AUTO_TEST_CASE` instances: `package_selection`, `sigops_adjusted_weight_chunk_limit`, `basic_mining`, and `prioritised_mining`. Each test case constructs its own 110-block fixture chain using a shared `MineBlockInfoChain` helper. In `basic_mining`, test transactions are now instantiated declaratively instead of mutating a single shared transaction object across sections, and `submitSolutionOld7` now tests the exact error message.",
  "problem": "Subtests in `CreateNewBlock_validity` shared a single in-memory chain, forcing later subtests to inherit state from earlier ones and requiring manual adjustments to `Tip()->nHeight` between calls. In `TestBasicMining`, a single `CMutableTransaction` was mutated across tests, making individual assertions depend on field modifications from prior checks and complicating isolation and debugging.",
